Current Dev Position: YP 5.0 M4 - Final Release

Next Deadline: 1st April 2024 YP 5.0 M4 build

Next Team Meetings:

   -

   Bug Triage meeting Thursday March 21st at 7:30 am PST (
   https://zoom.us/j/454367603?pwd=3DZGxoa2ZXL3FkM3Y0bFd5aVpHVVZ6dz09)
   -

   Weekly Project Engineering Sync Tuesday March 19th at 8 am PST (
   https://zoom.us/j/990892712?pwd=3DcHU1MjhoM2x6ck81bkcrYjRrcmJsUT09)
   <https://zoom.us/j/990892712>
   -

   Twitch -  See https://www.twitch.tv/theyoctojester


Key Status/Updates:

   -

   YP 5.0 M3 has been through QA. There is one major issue, we will likely
   release M3 and fix that in M4.
   -

   YP 4.0.17 is in QA.
   -

   There is a regression on beaglebone testing where X is no longer
   starting which was found during M3 QA. Fixes are under discussion for th=
is
   and will be in M4.
   -

   A key worry now is the documentation for the release, especially given
   it is an LTS. There are emails on the docs list about this, help is much
   appreciated.
   -

   The opkg lock issue with systemd images continues to be a significant
   concern for the release. We do now have a way to reproduce the bug and i=
t
   is due to =E2=80=9Copkg configure=E2=80=9D being executed in a postinsta=
ll script whilst
   opkg install has the lock.
   -

   There is a uninative issue showing up with newer distros due to the
   glibc changes where the pthread library is no longer separate. There are
   patches in testing to try and mitigate against this.
   -

   There are multiple other failures occurring on the autobuilder but no
   specific pattern has been identified as yet. One test build had 4 differ=
ent
   failures, and 2 of them were new never seen before issues. There is also
   some kind of issue with devtool/recipe tool test isolation in selftest
   which needs to be tracked down.
   -

   The previously reported CVE database update issue has been mitigated for
   now but further improvements to the autobuilder process for generating t=
he
   metrics may still be needed.


Ways to contribute:

   -

   As people are likely aware, the project has a number of components which
   are either unmaintained, or have people with little to no time trying to
   keep them alive. These components include: devtool, toaster, wic, oeqa,
   autobuilder, CROPs containers, pseudo and more. Many have open bugs. Hel=
p
   is welcome in trying to better look after these components!
   -

   There are bugs identified as possible for newcomers to the project:
   https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers
   -

   There are bugs that are currently unassigned for YP 5.0. See:
   https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Medium+_5.0_Unassigned_Enh=
ancements/Bugs
   -

   We=E2=80=99d welcome new maintainers for recipes in OE-Core. Please see =
the list
   at:
   http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/meta/conf/distro/include/=
maintainers.inc
   and discuss with the existing maintainer, or ask on the OE-Core mailing
   list. We will likely move a chunk of these to =E2=80=9CUnassigned=E2=80=
=9D soon to help
   facilitate this.
   -

   Help is very much welcome in trying to resolve our autobuilder
   intermittent issues. You can see the list of failures we=E2=80=99re cont=
inuing to
   see by searching for the =E2=80=9CAB-INT=E2=80=9D tag in bugzilla:
   https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-INT.
   -

   Help us resolve CVE issues: CVE metrics
   <https://autobuilder.yocto.io/pub/non-release/patchmetrics/>
   -

   We have a growing number of bugs in bugzilla, any help with them is
   appreciated.
   -

   Regarding bugs, even if you can=E2=80=99t fix a bug, submitting a failin=
g test
   case that can reproduce the issue significantly improves the chances it
   might get fixed.


YP 5.0 Milestone Dates:

   -

   YP 5.0 M3 is ready for release.
